<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Clement VIII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1536">1536</a>–<a href="/years/1605">1605</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ippolito Aldobrandini</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Clement VIII reigned from 1592 to 1605. He absolved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV of France</a> in 1595 and brought the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> under direct papal rule in 1598, refusing to recognise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-d-este-duke-of-modena">Cesare d'Este</a> as heir. He also issued the Clementine Vulgate and raised small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fief">fiefs</a> such as Masserano to principalities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-clement-viii.jpg" alt="Pope Clement VIII" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gelindu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1280282369_clement-viii.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Pope Clement VIII</b> refused to recognise his cousin Cesare, and in 1598 Ferrara passed to the Papal States.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-ferrara">Duchy of Ferrara</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1598 <b>Pope Clement VIII</b> raised them to a principality held as a fief of the Holy See, giving the family sovereign status.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-masserano">Principality of Masserano</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fano">Fano</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.84,13.01&amp;year=1580" aria-label="Fano on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4862 610 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Pope Clement VIII"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5312 880h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5312 880h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=43.84,13.01&amp;year=1580">What was here in 1580? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
